# Future work — features/editor/chrome

- `overlayRect` under CSS `zoom`. `getBoundingClientRect()` is zoom-scaled, while
  `clientLeft`/`clientTop` and `scrollLeft`/`scrollTop` are not, so a zoomed manuscript
  ancestor breaks the conversion (a Chromium probe at `zoom: 1.25` missed by 73px across and
  48.125px down). No ancestor is zoomed today. Editor zoom would need an explicit scale
  conversion and a real-browser test: a jsdom suite stubs both readings.
